t is exactly that collection's item fields\n(single-segment paths only), and the outer allowlists are NOT reachable. When outside,\nitem fields are NOT reachable. The `@`-data check matters: handlebars parses `@index` as a\n`PathExpression` with `data: true`, which the current segment-based check would not catch.\n\n### 5. Render-context projection and omission\n\nProject `chats` at the **TOP LEVEL**, never under `user`. This is load-bearing, not\nstylistic: nesting it under `user` would make `{{#if user}}` true for an owner who has\nchats but authored no personalization, rendering an operator's personalization framing\nprose around no content. There is a required test for exactly this (task 1.9).\n\nOmission mirrors the existing three-level `userContext` discipline:\n- an entry's `excerpt` with no value is omitted from that entry\n- a collection that is empty or absent is omitted entirely (never an empty array — an\n  empty array is truthy, so `{{#if chats.recent}}` would wrongly pass)\n- `chats` itself is omitted when **neither collection** would render — including its\n  metadata scalars, which have no meaning with nothing listed\n\n### 6. Neutralization split\n\n- The five metadata scalars: `escapeForPrompt` (the strict `&<>` escape), like model and\n  account-identity values. They are server-computed numbers and dates.\n- **All four item fields** (`title`, `date`, `messageCount`, `excerpt`): `sanitizeAuthoredText`,\n  the tag-balance sanitizer. The spec is explicit that rendered digest item values take the\n  two tag rules. `messageCount` is stringified first.\n\nReuse the existing `promptValue(raw, neutralize)` helper — it already encodes the\nabsent/empty/trim omission rule and returns a `SafeString` from the created environment.\nDo NOT patch `Handlebars.Utils.escapeExpression`; the file comment explains why\n(`Handlebars.create()` shares `Utils` by reference process-wide).\n\n### 7. Reserved delimiter\n\nAdd `user_chat_history` to `RESERVED_TAG_NAMES` in `a